# Blueprints and Things Built From Them

**The idea: a class is a blueprint. An object is one thing built from it.**

Like a cookie cutter and the cookies. One cutter, many cookies. Each cookie is its own cookie.

```cpp
class BobaCafe {
    int num_drinks_served;        // private: hidden inside
public:
    Drink doOrder(const std::string& customer_name);   // public: anyone can call
};
```

![one class and two objects built from it](courses/diagrams/e1e9c215-66b6-55eb-8d65-fc8d064efe01/objects.svg)

Each object (also called an **instance**) gets its **own copy** of the member variables.

**Check:** two cafes are built from one class. How many `num_drinks_served` variables exist?

