lessons.readme:
# Reversing a List Recursively

**The idea: each call remembers the node before it, and points itself back at that node.**

Lecture Example 3:

```cpp
Node* reverseHelper(Node* ptr, Node* last) {
    if (ptr->next == nullptr) {
        ptr->next = last;
        return ptr;           // old tail = new head
    }
    Node* newHead = reverseHelper(ptr->next, ptr);
    ptr->next = last;
    return newHead;
}

Node* reverse(Node* ptr) {
    if (ptr == nullptr) return ptr;
    return reverseHelper(ptr, nullptr);
}
```

For 1 → 2 → 3: calls `(1, null)`, `(2, 1)`, `(3, 2)`.

