# Coding a Circular Deque

**The idea: the circular queue, plus two backward moves. Always add N before `%`.**

![f and r stepping backward around the array](courses/diagrams/468a5e04-b897-5334-80ca-90383ad5df75/steps.svg)

```cpp
// insertFront: step back, then write
f = (f - 1 + N) % N;
Q[f] = e;

// removeBack: step back, then read
r = (r - 1 + N) % N;
return Q[r];

// last: look one behind r
return Q[(r - 1 + N) % N];
```

Without `+ N`, C++'s `%` gives −1, and you index `Q[-1]`.

> [!note]
> Lab 6 makes this growable. Its bonus uses a deque of indices for sliding-window max in O(n).

## Assignment

Give the print desk its deque. It has a fixed size, so it throws when full.

1. [ ] `insertFront(v)`: throw `FullDequeException()` when full.
2. [ ] `removeBack()`: remove and return the last job, or throw `EmptyDequeException()`.
3. [ ] `last()`: return the last job without removing it, or throw.

